abstract: >
  A Python verification harness for the finite audit of Paper SE-210,
  Operational Identity.
  Three independent derivations of the audit (an explicit-relation oracle,
  a partition-label procedure, and an edge characterization) read the same
  raw data and share only data classes.
  The harness checks them against each other, against the paper's cases,
  against properties the paper states, and against conformance vectors
  checked by the Lean formalization.
  It provides evidence, not proof.

